# StudyZone — AI-powered academic command center

## Core stack (DO NOT CHANGE)

- Frontend: React + Vite, JavaScript
- Styling: Tailwind CSS; shadcn/ui where useful; Lucide React icons
- Backend: Node.js serverless APIs (Vercel-compatible)
- Database & auth: Supabase PostgreSQL + Supabase Auth
- AI: Gemini API (server-side only)
- Deploy: Vercel; repo: GitHub

## Architecture

- No Next.js, no alternate frontend, no Firebase/MongoDB, no Python/Docker
- No `app.listen()` production servers — use Vercel serverless functions
- Never expose Gemini keys or Supabase service-role credentials in client code
- Use env vars for secrets; never hardcode localhost in production
- Keep dependencies minimal

## UI

- Premium SaaS style; responsive; accessible forms/nav/buttons
- Consistent spacing, typography, hierarchy; Lucide icons
- Loading, empty, and error states required
- Avoid generic AI dashboards, excessive gradients/glassmorphism/animation

## Development

- Inspect before modifying; reuse components; keep `App.jsx` thin
- No duplicate components; no unnecessary rewrites
- Run build/lint after significant changes; fix errors, don't hide them
- Never claim a feature works without testing it

## Incremental delivery

Build one requested feature at a time: inspect → plan briefly → implement only that feature → run checks → report changes. Do not add unrequested features.

## Full-stack scope (future)

Auth, subjects, tasks, deadlines, dashboard stats, productivity tracking, AI study planning, persistent Supabase data, secure backend APIs, Vercel deployment.
